WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Backhand volley for complete beginners.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.920
From the grip to the bouncing feet and the whole ready position, forehand and backhand volleys are the same.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:13.440
The backhand backswing must not be big either: tilt the racket face back slightly and keep the racket in front of you.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.048
With the racket back you can even see the face behind you.

00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:19.900
When you hit, the body slides forward like a wall.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.045
Again lead to the ball with the handle, keep the wrist firm all the way,

00:00:24.045 --> 00:00:26.360
spread both elbows outward and stamp your right foot as you hit.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.780
The lower the ball, the more open the racket face.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.000 line:10%
Observation area

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.780
The higher the ball, the more closed the racket face.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.000 line:10%
Observation area

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.040
With the basics in place, we start the basic fixed-point drills.
